\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The reversed chart equals the increasing Pfaffian}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Use the reversed volume of \ref{fdip-00MB} and the increasing
matching scalar of \ref{fdip-00MD}. The identity proved in
\ref{fdip-008J} is
##{I_\xi\left(e^{-\frac12\xi^TA\xi}\right)
 =\operatorname{Pf}(A).}
The top term of #{e^{-\Omega}} contributes #{(-1)^m}. Reversing
#{2m} generators contributes
#{(-1)^{m(2m-1)}=(-1)^m}. Those two signs cancel, so the reversed
coefficient equals the increasing Pfaffian. Singular #{A} is
included. If #{A} is invertible, then #{\operatorname{Pf}(A)\ne0}.}
